        <mxCell id="finding" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Finding:&lt;/b&gt; [Report ID, expected department, observed department, source IDs. Use 2–3 sentences.] In W06-S02, CJ-603, CJ-604, AND CJ-607 all have asset types that are of DRAIN and their required destination is the drainage department according to the approved destination policy in W06-S03 but they were not sent to that department. In the delivery logs in W06-S04, it shows that these reports were received by electrical every time which shows issues in incorrect routing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Unanswered question:&lt;/b&gt; [What evidence would help establish the cause?] Something that would help understand the cause would be to check how resolve destination is reading routing entries from D2 Routing Table and if the D2 routing table is giving correct information to the resolve destination. This would need to be checked with the service administrator that maintains the table." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="1089" x="40" y="585" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
